 **Where it runs:** on planned names at the blueprint stage; on every monday text payload immediately before its write; on everything in `drafts/`, which is all client-facing, the recap and the admin checklist alike; on `sop/` after every update **and before the diagrams are rendered**, so a rendered image can only carry text the lint has already seen; on the text **and the document properties** extracted from the rendered Word and PDF, because author, company and title fields travel with the file; on the doc-copy text read back; on live object names during the audit; and on `sop/` and `deliverables/` again at close-out.
 
-**What it blocks, and never auto-fixes:** the consultancy, plugin and assistant names; client-derived cost figures in any common format (45000, 45,000, 45k, $45k, "forty-five thousand"); any run of six or more consecutive words copied from an internal file; client quotes of eight or more words; evidence markers and internal ids in context; method vocabulary; objection text, stakeholder assessments and alternatives in play; other clients' names, matched against the hashed index; record paths, HTML comments and raw monday ids of eight or more digits outside links; and the three categories a paraphrase carries past the copied-run rule: personal and emotional stakes, closing tactics (deadline anchors, cost-of-waiting math, planned commitment questions, exit-ramp notes) and remarks by client staff about colleagues. Those three are also kept out of the client-safe block at the moment `call-intake` writes it, because that block is exempt from the copied-run rule. The full list of what client-facing material never contains is method §7, linked from `shared/sales-method.md`; the lint enforces what a string rule can reach, and the authoring rules (one tool category per sentence outside a call folder) are `sop-writing.md`'s to enforce.
