-**Exemptions that make the progressive SOP possible:** the marked client-safe block in each call summary and in each document snapshot, the blueprint's client-safe glossary, and any run that matches the text of a client document in `inputs/` are exempt from the copied-run rule, because they are written for the client in the first place or by the client; the rest of a document snapshot stays inside the rule. Runs made mostly of common words are ignored. Warnings, not blocks: other numbers, and personal names absent from the SOP's role and approver tables. The per-client allowlist (`solution/allowlist.md`) clears vocabulary rules only, never figures, copied runs, quotes, markers, ids or other clients' names, and every row needs the user's OK.
